{"text": "Lindenmuth Trial Lawyers, P.C. | Privileged settlement communication\n\nLindenmuth Trial Lawyers, P.C.\n900 S. Gay Street, Suite 1150 · Knoxville, Tennessee 37902 · (865) 555-0134 · tql@lindenmuthtrial.example\nNovember 3, 2025\nVIA EMAIL AND CERTIFIED MAIL (corinne.maddock@plumblinemutual.example)\nCorinne Maddock, Senior Claims Specialist\nPlumbline Mutual Insurance Company\nP.O. Box 30418, Nashville, TN 37241-0418\nRe: Your insured: Harlan Stubblefield · Claim No. PLM-HO-2025-0061847 · Policy HO3-7745120-02 · Date of loss: 07/26/2025 · Our client: M.C., a minor, by his mother and next friend Yesenia Covarrubias\nFOR SETTLEMENT PURPOSES ONLY — Rule 408\nDear Ms. Maddock:\nThis firm represents Mateo Covarrubias, who is seven years old, and his mother. Mateo was born August 14, 2018 and is a second grader at Pellissippi Trace Elementary. Please treat this letter as our time-limited demand under the policy issued to Mr. Stubblefield.\nFacts\nOn the evening of Saturday, July 26, Mateo was riding his scooter on the sidewalk in front of your insured's home at 4127 Tooles Bend Court in Farragut. Your insured's dog, a 90-pound Rottweiler mix that was not on a leash and not behind a fence, knocked Mateo down and bit him in the face. A neighbor, Lucero Pineda, pulled the dog off. Animal control report no. AC-25-03391 records that the same dog bit a delivery driver in 2023. Liability under Tenn. Code Ann. § 44-8-413 is not in serious question.\nInjuries and treatment\nSmoky Ridge Children's Hospital emergency department, 7/26/25, MRN SR-4471209: three puncture wounds to the right cheek and a 4 cm laceration through the upper lip, closed with 14 sutures under sedation (billed as CPT 12013 and related codes).\nDr. Imogen Vasbinder of Vasbinder Facial Plastics saw Mateo on Aug. 12 and September 30. She expects a permanent, visible scar and recommends scar revision surgery at about age twelve, estimated at $14,800.\nSince the attack Mateo has nightmares and will not go near dogs; his pediatrician has diagnosed an adjustment disorder with anxiety and referred him for counseling.\nSpecial damages to date\nProvider\tDates\tCharges\nSmoky Ridge Children's Hospital\t7/26/25\t$9,412.37\nDr. Vasbinder\t8/12 – 9/30\t$1,150.00\nCounseling (6 visits)\tSept – Oct\t$780.00\nFuture scar revision (estimate)\t—\t$14,800.00\nTotal\t\t$26,142.37\n\nMateo is covered by TennCare (member ID ZTN 4409 2218 7), which has paid $3,906.11 and will assert a subrogation interest.\nDemand\nIn light of permanent facial scarring to a seven-year-old, we demand $185,000.00 (one hundred eighty-five thousand dollars) in full settlement. This offer remains open until 5:00 p.m. Eastern on December 5, 2025. Any settlement will require court approval because the claimant is a minor. Ms. Covarrubias can be reached only through this office; please do not contact her at 865-555-0177 again.\nVery truly yours,\nTobias Q. Lindenmuth (BPR No. 031877)\nTQL/lp\n\nClaim PLM-HO-2025-0061847 | Demand of November 3, 2025", "kind": "Word document", "detail": "462 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Corinne Maddock", "Harlan Stubblefield", "Mateo Covarrubias", "Yesenia Covarrubias", "Lucero Pineda", "Dr. Imogen Vasbinder", "Mateo", "Tobias Q. Lindenmuth", "Ms. Covarrubias"], "companies": ["Lindenmuth Trial Lawyers, P.C.", "Plumbline Mutual Insurance Company", "Smoky Ridge Children's Hospital", "Vasbinder Facial Plastics", "TennCare", "BPR", "TQL/lp"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Knoxville", "Tennessee", "Nashville", "Farragut", "Pellissippi Trace Elementary", "Tooles Bend Court"], "health": ["nightmares", "adjustment disorder", "anxiety", "puncture wounds", "laceration", "scar", "revision surgery", "facial scarring"], "sensitive": [], "names": ["Corinne", "Harlan", "Mateo", "Yesenia", "Tobias", "Ms."]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 3, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 3.600000001490116, "modelMs": 0